@startuml
title Additional roles migration

participant "DBaaS Adapter" as Adapter
participant "DBaaS Aggregator" as Aggregator
database "DBaaS Registry" as Registry

note over Adapter, Aggregator
  Starts when physical database registration answers 202 Accepted
  with the first portion of logical databases (up to 100).
end note

loop while Aggregator answers 202 Accepted
  Adapter -> Adapter: create users for new roles\nin logical databases of the portion
  Adapter -> Aggregator: report portion result\nPOST /api/v3/dbaas/{type}/physical_databases/{phydbid}/instruction/{instructionId}/additional-roles\n(connection properties of new users, or failure)

  opt adapter created users
    Aggregator -> Registry: save connection properties of logical databases\nand remove them from the migration plan
  end

  alt adapter reports failure, or saving results fails
    Aggregator -> Registry: delete migration plan
    Aggregator --> Adapter: 500 Internal Server Error (no error code): migration aborted,\nrestarts on next registration
  else portion is processed without failures
    alt logical databases remain in the plan
      Aggregator --> Adapter: 202 Accepted: next portion of logical databases
    else all logical databases are migrated
      Aggregator -> Registry: apply the parked registration request:\nsave new supported roles of physical database\nand delete migration plan
      Aggregator -> Aggregator: reset the adapter client and physical database caches
      note right of Aggregator
        The physical database enters the new state only here.
        Until this step it keeps the old set of roles, so the
        aggregator never hands out a role that is not yet stored
        in the DBaaS Registry. After the cache reset, requests use
        the new roles, adapter address and credentials.
      end note
      Aggregator --> Adapter: 200 OK: migration completed
    end
  end
end

legend bottom right
  Solid arrow: synchronous request. Dashed arrow: response.
  Each loop iteration is a separate request initiated by the adapter.
  Registry write acknowledgements are omitted.
endlegend
@enduml

